   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "CorridorKey 2.0 - how to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "1. Paste the path of your green-screen clip in \"Load Video (Path)\".\n   Linear EXR plates: use a Load Images (Path) node instead and set input_colorspace = linear.\n2. First run downloads ~5 GB of weights into models/corridorkey2/.\n3. Optional hint (white = subject): load a matte, convert it with \"Convert Image to Mask\"\n   and connect it to hint_mask. 1 frame = first-frame hint, N frames (= clip length) = per-frame hint.\n4. Outputs: foreground is straight (un-premultiplied); alpha is a MASK where 1 = subject.\n   ComfyUI's JoinImageWithAlpha inverts masks: put an InvertMask before it.\n5. For EXR/comp work set output_colorspace = linear (unclamped scene-linear)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "1. Paste the path of your green-screen clip in \"Load Video (Path)\".\n   Linear EXR plates: use a Load Images (Path) node instead and set input_colorspace = linear.\n2. First run downloads ~5 GB of weights into models/corridorkey2/.\n3. Optional hint (white = subject): load a matte, convert it with \"Convert Image to Mask\"\n   and connect it to hint_mask. 1 frame = first-frame hint, N frames (= clip length) = per-frame hint.\n4. Outputs: foreground is straight (un-premultiplied); alpha is a MASK where 1 = subject.\n   ComfyUI's JoinImageWithAlpha inverts masks: put an InvertMask before it.\n5. For EXR/comp work set output_colorspace = linear (unclamped scene-linear)."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
